  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bharat vs Union on 10 February, 2012 Author: Bhaskar Bhattacharya Bench: Bhaskar Bhattacharya Gujarat High Court Case Information System Print Sca/1560/2012 3/ 3 Order Bharat vs Union on 10 February, 2012 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/33997645/ 1 In The High Court Of Gujarat At Ahmedabad Special Civil Application No. 1560 of 2012 ========================================================= Bharat Foods Co-Op. Ltd - Petitioner(s) Versus Union Of India & 2 - Respondent(s) ========================================================= Appearance : Mr Gl Raval, Ld.Senior Advocate With Dipen Desai for Petitioner.",
    "facts": "Although it is contended that the order passed by the Commissioner of Customs (Appeals) in the case of Gokul Refoils and Solvents Limited, is not binding upon the Commissioner of Customs, Kandla, at the same time, it is admitted in the affidavit that the Assistant Commissioner of Customs (Port), Custom House, Kolkata, by his letter dated February 07, 2012 has informed that the order in Appeal No.KOL/CUS/CKP/213/2011 passed by Shri V.K. Puri, Commissioner (Appeals), Kolkata has been accepted by the Committee of Commissioners where the same issue involved in this application, has been decided against the Revenue.",
